12767	{"artifactId":"LLD-7e0ae92e8f3d3c3e-s3","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-7e0ae92e8f3d3c3e-s3-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T06:40:55.215Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DEF S003/ac1 (reviewed coverage inventory for Web, Mobile-iOS and Mobile-Android across the ten PRD domains) is designed as a 30-cell rubric over CORPUS_DOMAINS × UiType, with human editorial review of every passing cell.","evidence":"DEF.md:104 lists the ten domains and three platforms. contracts.ts:8-11 defines exactly those 10 CORPUS_DOMAINS and UI types 'web'|'mobile-ios'|'mobile-android'. HLD.md:48 requires that publication reject any missing cell, gap cell or failed evaluation, and that human editorial review assess every passing cell. LLD §2.1/§3.2 require 30 cells, reject gaps and duplicates, and require a matching human decision for each pass cell. [files: docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/DEF.md, src/design/corpus/contracts.ts, docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DEF S003/ac2 (unreviewed generated/inferred content is never presented as published source-authored guidance) is designed: inferred authorship survives review, and drafts cannot ship. Installation and retrieval, which belong to S004/S005, are not built here.","evidence":"DEF.md:105 states ac2. LLD §3.5 keeps provenance.authorship='inferred' after review, and §3.7 keeps installation, catalog and default state with S004/S005. validate.ts:81-82 already rejects non-reviewed records in publication mode, so the 'drafts cannot ship' path reuses an existing check. [files: docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/DEF.md, src/design/corpus/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S001's candidateContentDigest omits only releaseId, reviewDigest and the digest of the single coveragePath entry, and returns '' when that entry is missing or duplicated. This makes it safe to fill a placeholder coverage digest after computing the candidate digest.","evidence":"canonical.ts:96-106: `if (coverage.length !== 1) return '';` then deletes releaseId, reviewDigest and coverage[0].digest before hashing. This matches the normative order in HLD.md:42. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing coverage-envelope check in validateRelease is opaque except for the candidate binding, the reviewDigest and a ban on releaseId self-references. Strict sc4 semantics therefore have to come from S003.","evidence":"validate.ts:273-301 (validateCoverageEnvelope) only checks envelope.candidateContentDigest === candidateDigest, scans for any 'releaseId' key or value equal to manifest.releaseId, and compares reviewContentDigest(envelope) to manifest.reviewDigest. [files: src/design/corpus/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An inferred record keeps its label after review as long as it carries an explicit author and rationale.","evidence":"validate.ts:41-45 accepts authorship 'inferred' without sourceRefs only when the rationale matches /\\bindependently\\s+(?:authored|inferred|developed)\\b/i. Otherwise it raises provenance.incomplete. The design is consistent with this, but the seed authors need to know about the regex: an inferred record whose rationale lacks that phrase and has no sourceRefs will fail S001. [files: src/design/corpus/validate.ts]","action":"Optionally state the S001 rationale-phrase requirement for inferred seed records in §3.5/§3.6.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused S001/S002 surfaces exist with the stated shapes: StageAssessment {stage:'eligibility'|'coverage',candidateContentDigest,passed,issues}, checkPublication(candidate: unknown, assessments: unknown): PublicationCheck, prepareEligibilityCandidate(manifest, outputs, review) returning ValidationResult<EligibilityCandidate>, reviewContentDigest, releaseContentDigest, and CORPUS_LIMITS (10,000 files / 64 MiB / depth 64 / 1 MiB record).","evidence":"contracts.ts:57-60 STAGE_ASSESSMENT_SCHEMA; validate.ts:308 `export function checkPublication(candidate: unknown, assessments: unknown): PublicationCheck`; sources/assessment.ts:124 prepareEligibilityCandidate, which returns {manifest, files, assessment} and requires exactly one coverage entry (line 129); canonical.ts:5 `CORPUS_LIMITS = { recordBytes: 1024*1024, packageBytes: 64*1024*1024, files: 10_000, depth: 64 }`; canonical.ts:107-114 the digest helpers. [files: src/design/corpus/contracts.ts, src/design/corpus/validate.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/assessment.ts, src/design/corpus/canonical.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The CoverageReport/CoverageCell types and the coverage/ modules are new and do not already exist in code.","evidence":"A grep for CoverageReport|CoverageCell under src/design/corpus returned no matches. The only coverage logic is S001's opaque envelope check in validate.ts:274. The sc4 shape in the LLD matches HLD.md:119-120 exactly. [files: src/design/corpus/validate.ts, docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed call sites (assessment-fixtures.ts:37, acceptance.test.ts) and the stated harness cover what the new pure coverage modules need. In particular, the existing isolation test does not already compile a coverage/ directory, so S003 must add its own harness.","evidence":"assessment-fixtures.ts:34-40 finalizeFixture is the current coverage-fill pattern; S003's finalizer replaces its fixture-only envelope. sources/__tests__/isolation.test.ts:20 compiles only `src/design/corpus/*.ts` and `src/design/corpus/sources/*.ts`, and corpus/index.ts re-exports only contracts/canonical/validate. A separate coverage/index.ts entry plus a 'fresh compiled pure module harness' (LLD §7 smoke) is therefore needed and is stated. No production caller exists yet; S004 consumes the coverage modules later. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/__tests__/assessment-fixtures.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/__tests__/isolation.test.ts, src/design/corpus/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Packaged S003 evaluation, specimen and editorial files can carry S002 original/inferred lineage without changing S002 contracts.","evidence":"sources/contracts.ts:37-38 ORIGINAL_OUTPUT_SCHEMA allows authorship 'original'|'inferred' with author and rationale. OUTPUT_BINDING_SCHEMA (32-34) allows 'imported'|'derived' with sourceIds. assessment-fixtures.ts:18-24 shows a candidate with an empty imports list and all outputs declared as originals, which matches the LLD's 'original/inferred-only seed' edge case. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/contracts.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/__tests__/assessment-fixtures.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Assessment against the final candidate stays bound across the placeholder → real coverage digest transition, because candidateContentDigest excludes the coverage entry digest and reviewDigest. Re-running eligibility on the final candidate therefore yields the same digest.","evidence":"canonical.ts:100-102 deletes releaseId, reviewDigest and the coverage entry's digest. sources/assessment.ts:63-71 structuralCandidate replaces the coverage bytes with a private envelope, so assessEligibility does not depend on S003's coverage content. isolation.test.ts:70-77 shows assessEligibility on a finalized manifest binds the same candidateContentDigest and passes checkPublication. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/assessment.ts, src/design/corpus/sources/__tests__/isolation.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S003 leaves sc1/sc2/sc3 and S004/S005 ownership unchanged. Placing the final reviewed package under src/assets/design-corpus/ while keeping drafts outside src/assets is consistent with the HLD.","evidence":"HLD.md:34: 'Author eligible ... records and notices under proposed src/assets/design-corpus/. Existing copy-assets.mjs copies src/assets recursively ... Ship only a validated reviewed release, never candidate downloads.' copy-assets.mjs:28 `const DIRS = ['prompts', 'assets'];` copies recursively. Keeping drafts in design/corpus-seed/v1 is a stricter reading that ensures drafts are not shipped. HLD.md:205 assigns bundled-package installation to S004, and the LLD §3.7 hands it off and does not install. [files: docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/HLD.md, copy-assets.mjs]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every diagnostic code the error paths name (inventory.invalid, domain.invalid, schema.invalid, reference.missing, review.stale, digest.mismatch, provenance.incomplete, review.required, assessment.failed, path.invalid, limit.exceeded) exists in the closed S001 ISSUE_CODES set. No new code is needed, and none would be accepted by STAGE_ASSESSMENT_SCHEMA.","evidence":"contracts.ts:53-55 ISSUE_CODES contains all eleven. VALIDATION_ISSUE_SCHEMA (line 56) is a closed union, and checkPublication decodes assessments against it (validate.ts:332). [files: src/design/corpus/contracts.ts, src/design/corpus/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A noncomputable candidate identity returns a ValidationResult failure rather than a malformed StageAssessment, mirroring S002.","evidence":"sources/assessment.ts:76-78: assessEligibility returns failure(inventory.invalid) when candidateContentDigest is ''. checkPublication marks every assessment assessment.stale when contentDigest is empty (validate.ts:342). [files: src/design/corpus/sources/assessment.ts, src/design/corpus/validate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both S003 acceptance criteria map to named tests, and the stated framework (node:test + node:assert/strict under tsx, fresh-compiled isolation harness) matches existing corpus tests.","evidence":"LLD §7 maps ac1 to coverage-matrix, evaluation-binding, seed-coverage and seed-bundle, and ac2 to editorial-binding and two candidate-coverage tests, which together cover the HLD.md:48 verification matrix for S003. Existing tests use node:test with node:assert/strict (isolation.test.ts:2-3) and a temporary-dir tsc compile with I/O denied (isolation.test.ts:11-86). [files: src/design/corpus/sources/__tests__/isolation.test.ts, docs/epics/di1-open-source-design-corpus-retrieval-E202610117e0ae92e/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T06:40:55.215Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
